    "lyrics": {
      "text": "Let the heav--ens re-joice;__ let earth-ly things be__ glad; for the Lord__ hath wrought might with His arm, He hath tram--pled up-on death by death. The first-born of the dead hath He be-come. From the bel-ly of Ha-des hath He de-liv-ered us, and hath grant--ed great mer-cy to the world. \n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho-ly Spir--it.\n\nBoth now and ev-er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nWe praise thee, the Me-di-a-tress for the sal-va-tion of our race, O Vir-gin The-o-to-kos; for in the flesh tak-en from thee, thy Son and our God hath deigned to en-dure the pas-sion through the Cross, and hath re-deemed us from cor-rup-tion, since He is the Friend of man.____"
    }
  }
